Use typed personal-ops actions instead of raw shell or generic MCP spelunking when the task is about calendar, mail, drive, bookmarks, or browser-auth readiness.

Available actions:
- `mail_search` — search the configured mailbox through IMAP
- `mail_read_thread` — load a thread/history by message ID
- `calendar_search` / `calendar_create` — routed to connected calendar MCP tools
- `drive_list` / `drive_export` / `drive_sync` — routed to connected drive MCP tools
- `bookmark_ingest` — routed to connected bookmark-capable MCP tools
- `browser_auth_status` — inspect browser profile/auth readiness

Mutation actions (`calendar_create`, `drive_sync`, `bookmark_ingest`) require `confirm_mutation=true` so the runtime can respect autonomy approval boundaries.
